    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite passes. Here's a summary.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Goal:** expose `telephoneDisplay` = the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\n1. **New `util/Telephones.java`** \u2014 a single home for E.164 country-code knowledge. It provides:\n   - `forDisplay(e164)` \u2014 splits off the recognized country calling code, then groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n   - `countryCode(e164)` and `isNationalLengthValid(e164)` \u2014 the country-code registry (`61`\u21929, `1`\u219210) and length check.\n\n2. **Deleted `rest/function/owner/E164CountryLength.java`** and pointed `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` at `Telephones.isNationalLengthValid`. Rather than copy the country-code table into a second place, I moved the create-path length rule and the new display formatter onto one shared source of truth (behavior is identical). The rationale comment about lenient canonicalization vs. strict create-time length moved into `Telephones`' javadoc.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default method delegating to `Telephones.forDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, wired via `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", ...)`, consistent with the other derived-field mappings. `telephone` is untouched, so it stays raw E.164.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n## Test results\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` **passes**: `$.telephone` = `+61412345678`, `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.\n- Full `mvn test`: **1/1 pass, BUILD SUCCESS** (the repo's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## One caveat to flag\n\n`mvn verify` fails on the JaCoCo coverage gate (line 0.21 vs. required 0.85). This is **pre-existing and structural**, not caused by my change: the repository contains a single acceptance test that exercises ~21% of the code, so the 85% line / 66% branch gate cannot be met regardless. The new `Telephones` code is itself exercised by the passing acceptance test. I did not weaken the gate or pad it with synthetic tests. If you'd like, I can add focused unit tests for `Telephones` (and/or the owner pipeline) to move coverage toward the gate.",
